# Development Workflow

## When asked to analyze or work on the project:
1. First explore the current codebase structure
2. Identify the relevant files and directories
3. Understand the existing patterns and conventions
4. Suggest improvements while maintaining consistency

## When creating new features:
- Start by understanding the existing architecture
- Follow established patterns in the codebase
- Consider backward compatibility
- Add appropriate documentation
- Include error handling

## When debugging:
- Check the console for errors first
- Look for existing error handling patterns
- Consider logging and debugging tools
- Test edge cases

## When refactoring:
- Maintain existing functionality
- Update related documentation
- Consider impact on other parts of the system
- Test thoroughly after changes
